# widget

[![CI](https://github.com/example/widget/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/example/widget/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
[![Go Reference](https://pkg.go.dev/badge/github.com/example/widget.svg)](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/example/widget)
[![Go Report Card](https://goreportcard.com/badge/github.com/example/widget)](https://goreportcard.com/report/github.com/example/widget)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

An example CLI.

## Install

```console
# Go toolchain
go install github.com/example/widget/cmd/widget@latest

# Homebrew (replace OWNER with your GitHub username once the tap is published)
brew install OWNER/tap/widget
```

Or download a prebuilt archive for your platform from the
[latest release](https://github.com/example/widget/releases/latest).

## Usage

```console
$ widget check input.txt
ok	input.txt
```

`widget` reads each input file (or stdin via `-` / a pipe), validates it,
and exits `0` if every input passes, `1` if any fails validation, or `2` for a
usage error. Use `-o json` for machine-readable output and `--help` for the full
flag set.

## Build from source

```console
$ git clone https://github.com/example/widget
$ cd widget
$ go build ./cmd/widget
$ go test ./...
```

